{
  "about": "Minimal per-pack schemas. Each names the top-level fields a pack must carry, the collections it must contain, and the fields every record in a collection must have. They were written from what the twelve packs already are, so they lock the shape rather than inventing one. A lane that produces a pack missing a collection something reads is stopped before the pack is written.",
  "min_records_note": "min_records is a floor at about four fifths of the count when the schema was written, not an exact count. It catches a collection emptying or being gutted, which is how a pack silently stops feeding a system, without failing every time somebody legitimately removes one record.",
